1
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:15,257
For now, it doesn't look like
anyone's trying to tail us.

2
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,820
Bucerati, shouldn't we be leaving Venice?

3
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,660
The boss commands a convoy of bodyguards.

4
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:24,157
Chances are they already know
about our betraying the Familia.

5
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,181
The next threat will likely turn
out to be someone from the inside.

6
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:33,233
The worst part is, we have no idea
what kind of torture they can dole out.

7
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,530
Certo.

8
00:00:34,613 --> 00:00:38,404
It's far too risky for our band
of defectors to take to the seas.

9
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,340
For now, we observe.

10
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,250
Understood.

11
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,170
Mister!

12
00:00:44,253 --> 00:00:45,083
We're hungry!

13
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,877
Hey, what are you waiting for?

14
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:47,790
Feed us!

15
00:00:47,873 --> 00:00:48,897
My guts are free!

16
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,440
What's with the hold up?

17
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,640
Where's the food?

18
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,010
Enough!

19
00:00:56,980 --> 00:01:01,921
I hate to ask this right now, but do you
think we have time to drop by a restaurant?

20
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:03,780
I suppose we do.

21
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,490
Okay, then.

22
00:01:07,573 --> 00:01:09,400
We should all fill our goat sauce.

23
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:40,760
Let's go.

24
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,157
Thank you

25
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:16,240
so

26
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:24,700
much for watching.

27
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:52,677
So, I was thinking, people that
are vegan, do they eat cheese?

28
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,348
Or does it, like, go against
one of their rules or something?

29
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:58,857
Uh, I'm pretty positive that they don't.

30
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:02,637
Products like milk and eggs come
from cows and chickens, remember?

31
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:07,080
And since you put milk in a cake,
that's a no-go as well. Wait, what?

32
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,777
They have to swear off cake too?

33
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,997
I wonder if all that health crap
really makes any difference.

34
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,492
So nothing from animals?

35
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,037
Then what do they do
about shoes or handbags?

36
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,397
All of that stuff is made
from leather, isn't it?

37
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,697
Look, they're vegan because
they feel bad for the animals.

38
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:25,420
They wear sneakers and carry
around backpacks instead.

39
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:26,620
Oh man!

40
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,040
They take this stuff so seriously!

41
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:33,517
So are there a bunch of vegan grannies
out there dressed like ballplayers?

42
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,894
Hey Giorno, fear won't do us any favors.

43
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,420
Try to relax and eat.

44
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:41,160
Sure, I'll try to, but we
all need to remain vigilant.

45
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,520
If not, someone could
easily poison our food.

46
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,270
Huh?

47
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,557
The hell are you doing,
you spindly little shit?!

48
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,517
What the...?

49
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:53,237
You think I'm gonna let
you get away with this?

50
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,797
This stain is gonna cost you!

51
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,000
My suit cost four million lira, pal!

52
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:58,848
Now I'm gonna make you pay!

53
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:05,600
So you're our next foe! What?

54
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:07,302
Don't hear you!

55
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,127
You trying to start trouble?

56
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:11,760
Take that, Katsune! And this! And this!

57
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,900
And one of these!

58
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,897
Hey, pump the brakes for a second.

59
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:20,977
I don't think this guy's an enemy.

60
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,160
He's out cold.

61
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:26,140
A random citizen. Go figure. What?

62
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,340
Are you for real?

63
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:29,521
Oh, shit, what am I gonna do now?

64
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,997
Yeah, sucks for you, but this
stain's not going anywhere.

65
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:37,097
Guess that's what happens when you mess
up and spill red wine on a white suit.

66
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,010
No way!

67
00:04:38,093 --> 00:04:39,317
I can pay for something this fancy!

68
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,457
Putting a button there
should cover it up nicely,

69
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:44,305
so good thing for you
the stain is where it is.

70
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Before we let this guy go, Let's
have them taste our food for poison

71
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:54,620
Enough, we don't have
time to mess around now

72
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,720
Something's not right What in the
world is going on with Bucciarati?

73
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:05,425
There's no question about it His heart
was stopped after his battle with the boss

74
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:10,489
And when he pierced his hand Not a single
drop of blood seeped from the wound

75
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:13,460
This whole thing is so confusing

76
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:18,777
But this really isn't the time to investigate
gate, since it's still just a feeling.

77
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,507
Letting the others know
wouldn't do any good.

78
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,080
Okay, Bucciarati.

79
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:26,224
What do we do from here on out?

80
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,780
The boss possesses the
power to obliterate time,

81
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:32,420
and only he can move when his ability

82
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:34,770
is activated.

83
00:05:34,853 --> 00:05:35,683
He is unstoppable.

84
00:05:35,766 --> 00:05:38,260
Doesn't matter the person or the approach.

85
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,430
His stand

86
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,337
is so powerful, attacks
have no effect in the least.

87
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,250
However...

88
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:48,060
All bets are off once
we unveil his identity.

89
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,277
After we finally figure
out who the boss really is,

90
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,595
we can eliminate him once and for all.

91
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:56,680
It'll be tough, but we've no other choice.

92
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:59,020
It's kill or be killed.

93
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:02,217
I'm with you, but how the
hell are we gonna find him?

94
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:06,594
The boss has made extra certain to
remove any trace of his life till now.

95
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,140
What about Trish?

96
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:12,957
Surely we can learn something useful
from her, given how involved she is.

97
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:16,628
Just think about how those goons
and the boss came after her.

98
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,010
You know?

99
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,480
Well, I've been thinking.

100
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,260
I don't like it.

101
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,857
We've already involved
Trish enough in this.

102
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:31,080
It just doesn't feel right.

103
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,105
Trish is the true victim here.

104
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,697
Knowing her own father tried to kill her.

105
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:36,997
Think how she must be feeling.

106
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:37,910
It's too much.

107
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:39,957
Have a heart, Bucciarati.

108
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:44,805
Involving her in the hunt for the boss
and his secret identity is the wrong move!

109
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,130
Thank you.

110
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:49,140
But it's okay, Narancia.

111
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,100
I've known all that.

112
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,540
About the kind of man he is.

113
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:54,820
My father.

114
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,600
T-Trish.

115
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,560
No, it's alright.

116
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,588
In fact, your talk of him leaving
no trace sparked something.

117
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,668
I wondered about my father.

118
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,038
So I asked Mom, and she said
she met him in Sardinia.

119
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,910
Sardinia.

120
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,500
When I was little, Mom told a story
that was very strange to me at the time.

121
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:18,879
They met while she was on vacation.

122
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:21,240
One day, he went to run an errand.

123
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:24,100
But he vanished and left nothing behind.

124
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,900
Not even his real name.

125
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,497
That must have been right
before he became the boss.

126
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:31,698
That far back, do you think
it could be his hometown?

127
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:33,240
I can't say for sure.

128
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,640
But, it's somewhere to start.

129
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:39,964
Sardinia holds the key
to his past and identity.

130
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,817
You know what telling us that means?

131
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:44,997
We very well might end up
killing your biological father.

132
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,760
No, we'll do all we can to bring him down.

133
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:52,849
Honestly, whether your group decides to
kill him or not is your own business.

134
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:55,300
There's only one thing I want to know,

135
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:58,381
and it's whose blood is
coursing through my veins!

136
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:01,892
I'll be damned if someone kills
me before I get an answer!

137
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:06,140
Look at that, Narancia.

138
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,115
Guess you were wrong.

139
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:12,477
This girl standing before us is way
tougher than you thought she was.

140
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,700
Fine, I get it.

141
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:16,290
Sardinia...

142
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,817
That's where we're heading
after we escape this place.

143
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,782
It's where we'll find out
who the boss really is.

144
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:31,337
Guess I was projecting too much onto
Trish and totally missed the mark.

145
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:34,277
It's clear she's already
found her Determinazione.

146
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:38,125
But given that I decided to join
this suicide mission on a whim,

147
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:41,749
I'm going into this thing with
more doubt than hope for now.

148
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:35,620
Ah Uh, guys, we've got company!

149
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:39,229
My soup's got a weird
shark swimming in it!

150
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,600
Lil' Bomber!

151
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,190
Joino, quick!

152
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,187
Get Trish inside the turtle!

153
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,820
Habakio, guard right! Mista, left!

154
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:49,397
Well, where are they?

155
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,877
Where are we being attacked from?

156
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,195
Inside the soup bowl.

157
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,537
I don't know how it got in there, though.

158
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:55,640
Are you serious?

159
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,800
But it was right there!

160
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:00,817
I swear there was some
shark-looking thing in my soup!

161
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:01,730
Huh?

162
00:10:01,813 --> 00:10:02,643
Huh?

163
00:10:02,726 --> 00:10:03,957
I'm not seeing anything strange here.

164
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:05,805
Did we lose the thing already?

165
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,020
Narancia, you okay?

166
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,470
What happened?

167
00:10:29,553 --> 00:10:30,797
What the heck are you screaming about?

168
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,710
What?

169
00:10:31,793 --> 00:10:32,623
Did that shark bite you?

170
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,515
Tell me what's wrong.

171
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:36,080
I can help. Talk to me!

172
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:41,048
I'm trying to help, but
you gotta answer me!

173
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,652
Hold on a moment, Mista.

174
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,780
Narancia may not be able to speak.

175
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,570
What?

176
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:48,302
Have you really lost your voice?

177
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:58,897
What's wrong, Narancia?

178
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:00,617
Just what are you pointing at?

179
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,641
Is it the water?

180
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,631
You want a drink of that?

181
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,817
Hey, guys, we're gonna
need some help over here.

182
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:16,417
Look, his tongue has been
ripped right out of his mouth.

183
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:18,618
I don't think he's breathing either.

184
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,161
This isn't good.

185
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:24,477
I can make a replacement for
his tongue using Golden Wind,

186
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,337
but it'll take a little time to do it.

187
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,377
We don't have time.

188
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:29,877
Can't you see that Naranj
is about to suffocate?

189
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,842
Mista, do you have a pen on you?

190
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,490
Pen?

191
00:11:33,573 --> 00:11:36,020
Yeah, it's right here, but
what do you need it for?

192
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,840
Oh man, that was close.

193
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:56,519
I'll imbue the pen with life force
and create the replacement tissue.

194
00:11:56,900 --> 00:12:00,077
That way, he'll be able to
breathe through the process.

195
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:02,260
It all makes sense now.

196
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,100
That's Giorno Giovanna.

197
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:14,380
This is very interesting indeed, and
it explains the boss's intel reports.

198
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:18,780
So the greatest threat to the familia
comes from this cannoli-haired,

199
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:20,840
deadbeat newcomer. Yeah.

200
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:24,697
I have to admit, the brat keeping
Narancia alive was a surprise.

201
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:27,897
Never in my wildest dreams
would I have imagined Crush

202
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:31,156
having any trouble with this
particular assassination.

203
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:34,877
But apparently killing all
five of these reprobates

204
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:38,240
will necessitate your
involvement as well, Tiziano.

205
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:44,180
As the boss's elite guard, it is our duty
to ensure these turncoats perish here.

206
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:47,525
Are you ready to do what
must be done, Squalo?

207
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,340
Do you even need to ask?

208
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:53,660
Once I lure them into the water,
Crush will be unstoppable.

209
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,662
Our plan will decide everything.

210
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:59,220
Let's offer them one by one, Tiziano.

211
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,000
Gladly, Squalo.

212
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,920
And our friend Narancia is going to help.

213
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:17,260
Are you alright, Narancia? I'm good.

214
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:19,780
That was close.

215
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,537
What info can you give us?

216
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,500
Who are they?

217
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:23,957
How does their stand work?

218
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,500
It was in the soup bowl.

219
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:27,920
Some kind of shark.

220
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:32,660
Narancia, try to relax.
I'm fine. I can talk.

221
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,540
Hey, help us out.

222
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,217
What does the enemy look like?

223
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,476
Which way did he go?

224
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:38,830
He was...

225
00:13:38,913 --> 00:13:41,360
He was really small, like a huge pebble!

226
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,057
And he ran into the
back of the restaurant!

227
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:43,970
It was crazy!

228
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,170
Huh?

229
00:13:46,253 --> 00:13:47,860
How can a pebble be huge?

230
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:51,717
Weren't you saying just a few minutes
ago that you found it in your soup?

231
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,037
You're not making any sense.

232
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:53,950
What?

233
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:56,258
No, I didn't really say that, did I?

234
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,151
Here, answer this for me.

235
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:02,680
Would you say our foe's
about yay, Big? Nuh-uh.

236
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,357
No, wait, I...

237
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,793
Then would you say it's about this, Big?

238
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:11,937
It's bigger, so you're saying
it's something like this.

239
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:13,140
Yeah, you got it.

240
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:18,660
So this big-ass enemy was
taking a dip in your bowl,

241
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,797
then they just ran off into
the restaurant and vanished?

242
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,100
Mm-hmm. What the?

243
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,217
Why are they...

244
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:28,297
Sorry, but we're not quite understanding
the picture you're trying to paint.

245
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,377
You mean...

246
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:32,240
they move at extremely high speeds? No!

247
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,205
They're as slow as you can be!

248
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:35,960
Say what? Come on!

249
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:40,517
If it was as huge and slow as you
say, then why didn't we see it?

250
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,835
You sure you really saw Stan Narancia?

251
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,520
Of course I did!

252
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:46,200
Not see one!

253
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:48,510
Huh?

254
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:51,149
You're starting to
sound like a real wacko.

255
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,150
Hang on.

256
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:56,637
You're not trying to hide the fact that
